        <body>
            <div xml:id="d97">

                <pb facs="0208" n="146" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg146"/>

                <head>No. 92.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Holcombe to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-07-02"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 2, 1878</date>.
                        (Received September 2.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 20.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy
                    of a dispatch addressed by Prince Kung to Mr. Seward, proposing certain changes
                    in the regulations for foreign trade upon the Yangtze River.</p>
                <p>As the modifications suggested are manifestly to the advantage of <pb facs="0209"
                        n="147" xml:id="pg147"/> trade, I have replied to the prince assenting to
                    them. I inclose a copy of my dispatch to him, and also of one in which I have
                    notified the vice-counsul-general of my approval of the changes in question,</p>
                <p>Trusting that my course will meet with your assent,</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>CHESTER HOLCOMBE.</signed></closer>




